# Bot CLI in this project

This project was scaffolded with `--kind bot`: the standard MT5 compose
stack plus the files an AI trading overlay needs. The `qkt.config.yaml` here is
what `qkt bot` reads when run from this directory.

## Wire an AI agent

1. Bring the stack up (`make up`) and complete the one-time MT5 login (see README).
2. Give your agent shell access with this directory as its working directory.
3. Paste `SYSTEM_PROMPT.md` into the agent's system prompt and set its `--as` name.

## Smoke-test the surface by hand

```bash
qkt bot account --json
qkt bot quote MT5:XAUUSD --json
qkt bot buy 0.01 MT5:XAUUSD --sl by:5 --tp by:10 --dry-run --json   # offline preview
qkt bot buy 0.01 MT5:XAUUSD --sl by:5 --tp by:10 --as smoke --json  # real (demo!) order
qkt bot positions --json
qkt bot close MT5:XAUUSD --all --json
```

Every trade is journaled under the qkt state directory (`bot/<as>/journal-*.jsonl`)
and, when the `insights:` block is enabled, egressed to qkt-insights with the
canonical DSL text and its sha256.

Full reference: https://elitekaycy.github.io/qkt/reference/bot-cli/ (qkt {{QKT_VERSION}})
